                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \\underset{n}{\sum}
                  h_n
                  \\Big(
                  d \star_4 d V^{(n)} \wedge d x^4
                  +
                  \\left(
                  n + \tfrac{1}{2}
                  \\right)
                  \\star_{4} V^{(n)}
                  \-
                  \\sqrt{\tfrac{n+2}{2}\tfrac{n+1}{2}}
                  \\star_{4} V^{(n+2)}
                  \-
                  \\sqrt{\tfrac{n}{2}\tfrac{n-1}{2}}
                  \\star_4 V^{(n-2)}
                  \\Big)
                  \\wedge d x^4
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            Here the terms over the braces vanish because we have chosen
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorenz+gauge"} Lorenz gauge
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:4dLorenzGauge"} (5)
          %p
            Hence under the expansion
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HermiteExpansionOf5dVectorPotential"} (4)
            the 5d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxwell+equations"} Maxwell equations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mn 5
                  %mi d
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo ^
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \star_5 d \widehat A = 0
            become equivalently the following system of coupled equations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+Yang-Mills+theory"} massive Yang-Mills theory
            in 4d (using, with
            %a{:href => "Hodge+star+operator#HodgeStarFollowedByHodgeStar"} this Prop.
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+star+operator"} Hodge star operator
            on 3-forms in 4d squares to unity):
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mn 4
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mn 4
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo −
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mo )
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msqrt
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 2
                          %mn 2
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msqrt
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\star_4
                  d \star_4 d V^{(n)}
                  \\;=\;
                  \-
                  \\left(
                  n + \tfrac{1}{2}
                  \\right)
                  V^{(n)}
                  +
                  \\sqrt{\tfrac{n+2}{2}\tfrac{n+1}{2}}
                  V^{(n+2)}
                  +
                  \\sqrt{\tfrac{n}{2}\tfrac{n-1}{2}}
                  V^{(n-2)}
                  \\Big)
          %p
            Truncating this to the first term yields the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msqrt
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/\sqrt{2}
            (by
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "Hodge+star+operator#WaveOperatorOnMinkowskiSpacetime"} this Prop.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi μ
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\partial^\mu \partial_\mu V^{(1)}
                  \\;=\;
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}
                  V^{(1)}
                  \\,.
          %p
            More generally, truncating at some higher number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            of modes, one may find a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+transformation"} linear transformation
            among the fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{(n)}
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq n \leq N
            which diagonalizes
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SystemOfCoupledEquationsIn4d"} (8)
            to obtain a collection of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equations"} Klein-Gordon equations
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            massive fields.
          %p
            %br/
          %h4#SakaiSugimotoModel Sakai-Sugimoto model
          %p
            We discuss 5d Maxwell theory on the 5d spacetime that appears in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Sakai-Sugimoto model
            (from
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4%2FD8-brane+intersections"} D4/D8-brane intersections
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BolognesiSutcliffe13"} Bolognesi-Sutcliffe 13
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Sutcliffe15"} Sutcliffe 15
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            Consider 4d- and 5d-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            and equipped with global
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthonormal+basis"} orthonormal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+charts"} coordinate charts
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\{x^\mu\}, z\}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry"} isometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedding
          #eq:SakaiSugimotoSpacetime.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (9)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 3
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %msub
                                %mi ι
                                %mn 5
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 4
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi μ
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 3
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi κ
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 3
                          %mo ,
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathbb{R}^{3,1}
                  \&amp;\overset{\;\;\;\iota_5\;\;\;}{\hookrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\mathbb{R}^{4,1}
                  \\\
                  \\mu = &amp;   0, 1, 2, 3\;
                  \\\
                  \\kappa = &amp; 0, 1, 2, 3, &amp;&amp; z
                  }
          #SakaiSugimotoMetric.num_prop
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong (Sakai-Sugimoto metric)
            %p
              On the 5d manifold
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SakaiSugimotoSpacetime"} (9)
              the
              %em Sakai-Sugimito metric
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+tensor"} metric tensor
            #eq:SakaiSugimotoMetric.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (10)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi ν
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi μ
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi ν
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi d
                    %mi z
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi d
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    H^{+1} \, \eta_{\mu \nu} d x^\mu \otimes d x^\nu
                    +
                    H^{-1} d z \otimes d z
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mrow
                            %mi μ
                            %mi ν
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi diag
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\eta_{\mu \nu}) = diag(-1,+1,+1,+1)
                  is the metric of 4d
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                  given by
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi μ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo +
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi z
                                  %mn 2
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi L
                                  %mn 2
                            %mo )
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        H(\{x^\mu\}, z)
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        H(z)
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        \\left(
                        1 + \frac{z^2}{L^2}
                        \\right)^{2/3}
                %p
                  for some
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %p
            This metric is highlighted in this form in (
            %a{:href => "#BolognesiSutcliffe13"} Bolognesi-Sutcliffe 13, (2.1), (2.2)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Sutcliffe15"} Sutcliffe 15, (39), (40)
          #SakaiSugimotoEquation.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Sakai-Suimoto equation)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 4
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(\mathbb{R}^{4,1})
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-form"} differential 1-form
              on the spacetime
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SakaiSugimotoSpacetime"} (9)
              with vanishing
              = succeed "-component" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorenz+gauge"} Lorenz gauge
            #eq:VanishingzComponentOfVectorPotentialOnSSSpacetime.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (11)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi z
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A_z = 0
            #eq:LorenzGaugeForVectorPotentialOnSSSpacetime.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (12)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi μ
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi ν
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi ν
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial_\mu \eta^{\mu \nu} A_\nu = 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then the 5d vacuum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxwell+equations"} Maxwell equations
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+potential"} vector potential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+tensor"} metric tensor
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SakaiSugimotoMetric"} (10)
              are equivalent to
            #eq:SakaiSugomotoEquation.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (13)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⋆
                            %mi d
                            %mo ⋆
                            %mi d
                            %mi A
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi η
                              %mrow
                                %mi μ
                                %mi ν
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi μ
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi ν
                            %mi A
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo +
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi z
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msup
                                %mi H
                                %mrow
                                  %mn 3
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                  %mn 2
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi z
                              %mi A
                              %mo )
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \&amp;
                    \\star d \star d A
                    \\;=\;
                    0
                    \\\
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\;\;\;
                    \&amp;
                    \\eta^{\mu \nu}\partial_\mu \partial_\nu A
                    \\;+\;
                    H^{1/2}
                    \\partial_z
                    \\left(
                    H^{3/2} \partial_z A
                    \\right)
                    \\;=\;
                    0
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This equation is highlighted in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BolognesiSutcliffe13"} Bolognesi-Sutcliffe 13, (4.14)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Sutcliffe15"} Sutcliffe 15, (48)
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p Here is a somewhat lengthy computation:
            %p
              First notice the general component formula for the operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi d
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star d \star d
              applied to 1-forms, akin to, but different from, the component formula for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laplace-Beltrami+operator"} Laplace-Beltrami operator
              applied to 0-forms/functions (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Laplace+operator#LaplaceOperatorInComponents"} there
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⋆
                            %mi d
                            %mo ⋆
                            %mi d
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo ⋆
